      "label": "(b)",
      "marks": 4,
      "answer": "$x=-1-\\sqrt5i$ and $x=\\frac32$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "State the second root $-1-\\sqrt5i$ — B1.\n\nCarry out a complete method for finding a quadratic factor with zeros $-1+\\sqrt5i$ and $-1-\\sqrt5i$ — M1.\n\nObtain $x^2+2x+6$ — A1.\n\nObtain the remaining root $x=3/2$ — A1, OE.\n\nAlternative factor method: state $-1-\\sqrt5i$ — B1; use $(x+1-\\sqrt5i)(x+1+\\sqrt5i)(2x+a)=2x^3+x^2+6x-18$ — M1; use $(1-\\sqrt5i)(1+\\sqrt5i)a=-18$ — A1; $6a=-18$, $a=-3$, leading to $x=3/2$ — A1, OE.\n\nAlternative sum/product methods: state $-1-\\sqrt5i$ — B1. Either use POR $=6$ and SOR $=-2$ — M1, obtain $x^2+2x+6$ — A1, and $x=3/2$ — A1; or use POR $(-1-\\sqrt5i)(-1+\\sqrt5i)a=9$ — M1 A1 and obtain $x=3/2$ — A1; or use SOR $(-1-\\sqrt5i)+(-1+\\sqrt5i)+a=-1/2$ — M1 A1 and obtain $x=3/2$ — A1.\n\nTotal [4].",
